@database fuzzy.guide
@$VER: fuzzy.guide 0.1b1 (17.10.2026)
@author Tobias Karlsson

@node main "fuzzy.library"

@{b}fuzzy.library programmer's guide@{ub}

fuzzy.library does two things:

It works from C (and any language that can call a library) and from @{b}ARexx@{ub}.

This guide explains how to use it. Every call is described in full in the
@{"reference" link "reference"}. Working programs: tests/fuzzytest.c (C), tests/fuzzytest.rexx
(ARexx), and FuzzyFind's updatedb, locate and fzf.

@{b}The programmer's guide@{ub}

  @{"What you need" link "g-what-you-need"}
  @{"The first program" link "g-the-first-program"}
  @{"Matching" link "g-matching"}
  @{"How the ranking works" link "g-how-the-ranking-works"}
  @{"The index: reading and searching" link "g-the-index-reading-and-searching"}
